<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The banner's background: the ATLAS contour texture, tiled (W60, retextured W64).

  Source is `Test Files/splash.png` — a finer, more even contour field than the
  original. Tiled plain rather than mirrored: its two vertical edges differ by
  4.4/255 on average, so the repeat does not show, and mirroring would double the
  asset to hide a seam that is not there.

  ⚠️ `tileMode` repeats the bitmap at its **intrinsic** size, so the asset's
  density bucket is what decides how big the tile looks. It ships at xhdpi
  (640x256 px = 320x128 dp), which is the scale that read as texture rather than
  as an obviously repeating motif; Android rescales it for other densities.

  A `<bitmap>` rather than the flat `atlas_banner_field` colour it replaces.

  ⚠️ This is now the *only* thing behind the logo. The logo used to carry its own
  dark field and merely blend into this; since W66 it is transparent artwork, so
  the texture shows through it and any change here is visible around every letter
  — a lighter pattern would leave the chrome outlines with nothing to sit on.
-->
<bitmap xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:src="@drawable/atlas_pattern"
    android:tileMode="repeat" />
